","arithmetic-transport/movement.html":"<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Movement Observatory · PerfectPower</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#0a1722;color:#e4edf0;font:17px/1.65 system-ui}main{max-width:1060px;margin:auto;padding:28px 24px}a{color:#9ce6ce}h1{font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,58px);line-height:1.12;margin:30px 0 16px}.intro{max-width:750px;color:#b7cbd3}.panel{padding:25px;border:1px solid #294551;border-radius:20px;background:#102431;margin:22px 0}.controls,.stats{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}label{display:block;font-size:14px;color:#b7cbd3}select,button{font:inherit;background:#1c3743;color:white;padding:10px;border:1px solid #608575;border-radius:10px}.stat{flex:1;min-width:180px}.stat strong{display:block;font-size:32px;color:#a2e4ce}svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.legend{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:14px}.legend span{padding:4px 12px;border-radius:20px;color:#071920}.note{font-size:14px;color:#bbccd2}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#a2e4ce}#status{min-height:24px}button{cursor:pointer}button:focus,select:focus{outline:3px solid #d7ba82}</style></head><body><main><a href="/research">← Research laboratory</a><div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:28px">ORDER · PHASE · UNCERTAINTY</div><h1>What happened between<br>the stopwatch readings?</h1><p class="intro">Acceleration, braking, turning and recovery have an order. Explore several plausible interpretations of a movement rather than treating a single noisy boundary as certain.</p><section class="panel"><div class="controls"><div><label for="profile">Synthetic movement</label><select id="profile"></select></div><div><label for="temperature">How sharply the model favors a phase</label><select id="temperature"><option value="0.5">Sharper</option><option value="1" selected>Moderate</option><option value="2">Broader uncertainty</option></select></div><button id="save">Download exact-count experiment</button></div><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><label>Possible segmentations</label><strong id="count">—</strong></div><div class="stat"><label>Most likely interpretation</label><strong id="map">—</strong></div><div class="stat"><label>Uncertainty in first transition</label><strong id="width">—</strong></div></div><p class="note">These are public synthetic illustrations. Phase weights come from operational templates; they are not calibrated probabilities of a player's physiology. Counts are exact integers; weighted inference uses floating arithmetic.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Speed through the movement</h2><svg id="speed" viewBox="0 0 900 260" role="img" aria-label="Synthetic speed over time"></svg><p class="note">The vertical bands show the 5–95% model intervals for phase transitions. Their width measures boundary uncertainty.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Every frame has several possible explanations</h2><div class="legend"><span style="background:#92d8b8">Approach</span><span style="background:#dca5ad">Brake</span><span style="background:#a6b4e4">Redirect</span><span style="background:#f1d18f">Recover</span></div><svg id="phases" viewBox="0 0 900 220" role="img" aria-label="Probability of each operational phase at each frame"></svg><p class="note">The four phase weights sum to one at each frame. A blurred transition is useful information: the recording does not strongly distinguish those interpretations.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>From arithmetic paths to athlete movement</h2><p>PerfectPower counts and weights whole populations of allowed histories. The same finite-language machinery can represent all allowed phase boundaries, summarize their consequences and preserve event order. The private NFL adapter extracts features from Combine tracking and tests them with whole athletes held out.</p><p id="result">Loading current aggregate research evidence…</p><a href="https://github.com/towre676-cloud/perfectpower/blob/main/docs/MOVEMENT_LANGUAGE_MONOGRAPH.md">Read the engine and experiment account →</a><p class="note">An aggregate research improvement is separate from an established scouting advantage or a submitted Kaggle entry. Restricted athlete-level data is excluded from this demonstration.</p></section><p id="status" role="status"></p></main><script src="/arithmetic/movement-app.js"></script></body></html>
